# Public browser configuration only.
# Create your own Google Web OAuth client for your self-hosted PWA. This client
# ID is public and safe to ship to the browser. If durable Google authorization
# is enabled on your own Worker, GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID must be this same value.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com

# The Gemini API key is normally injected by the deployment/runtime boundary,
# not exposed as a Vite VITE_* value.

# Optional self-hosted lazy OCR assets. If unset, the OCR runtime uses its
# package default asset resolver without sending image content to a provider.
# VITE_OCR_ASSET_BASE_PATH=/assets/ocr

# Lazy BusyTeX assets required by document.create_pdf. Do not point this at a
# user-controlled URL; the compiler owns the configured runtime path.
# VITE_BUSYTEX_BASE_PATH=/core/busytex
